<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:aapt="http://schemas.android.com/aapt"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!-- The Gridlink 2x2 mark, dark mode. Ported verbatim from the vector master at
         ~/homelab/mail/branding/gridlink-icon.svg on Talos, the same file Forge and the
         webmail favicon come from, so this variant is the canonical one and the light twin
         in drawable/ is the derived one.

         Geometry is the Forge `.logo` rule (cells 14 / gap 4 / radius 3.5, so a 32-unit mark
         box) scaled by 1.375 to a 44-unit box centred on the 108 canvas: cells 19.25, gap
         5.5, radius 4.8125, origins at 32 and 56.75. Both variants share it exactly; if one
         moves, move the other and the monochrome layer with it.

         ⚠️ 44 is NOT the master's 43% of the canvas. The master is sized for a PWA tile,
         where the whole square is visible. An adaptive icon throws away the outer 18 on
         every side, so 43% of 108 would render as ~64% of what the user actually sees, i.e.
         far bigger than Forge. 44 of the visible 72 is 61%, which is what matches Forge on
         screen rather than on paper.

         🔴 Colours are pre-blended, never alpha. The two dim cells are rgba(74,144,217,0.4)
         over #06070a resolved by hand to #21405d. A 0.4-alpha fill renders as washed-out
         pastel instead of the muted navy it should be.

         The master's two feGaussianBlur glows have no VectorDrawable equivalent, so they are
         approximated with radial gradients that fade to transparent. They live in this
         layer, not the background, because launchers parallax the two layers independently
         and a glow that slides off its cell looks broken. -->

    <!-- ambient bloom under the top-left lit cell -->
    <path android:pathData="M17.625,17.625h48v48h-48z">
        <aapt:attr name="android:fillColor">
            <gradient
                android:type="radial"
                android:centerX="41.625"
                android:centerY="41.625"
                android:gradientRadius="24">
                <item android:offset="0" android:color="#4A4A90D9" />
                <item android:offset="0.4" android:color="#1C4A90D9" />
                <item android:offset="1" android:color="#004A90D9" />
            </gradient>
        </aapt:attr>
    </path>

    <!-- ambient bloom under the bottom-right lit cell -->
    <path android:pathData="M42.375,42.375h48v48h-48z">
        <aapt:attr name="android:fillColor">
            <gradient
                android:type="radial"
                android:centerX="66.375"
                android:centerY="66.375"
                android:gradientRadius="24">
                <item android:offset="0" android:color="#4A7CB2E6" />
                <item android:offset="0.4" android:color="#1C7CB2E6" />
                <item android:offset="1" android:color="#007CB2E6" />
            </gradient>
        </aapt:attr>
    </path>

    <!-- dim cell, top-right -->
    <path
